  {
    "id": "985d5685-4bff-34f6-ad5f-fd41d77a2c74",
    "content": {
      "id": "985d5685-4bff-34f6-ad5f-fd41d77a2c74",
      "contentType": "VIDEO",
      "title": "Apple iPhone revenue tops estimates, Services falls short",
      "description": "<p>Apple (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AAPL\">AAPL</a>) reported fiscal second quarter adjusted earnings of $1.65 versus a Bloomberg consensus estimate of $1.62. Revenue was $95.4 billion compared to the expected $94.6 billion. iPhone revenue was $46.8 billion. Wall Street had been anticipating $45.9 billion. Mac revenue and iPad revenue both topped estimates while Services and Wearables revenue fell short. Greater China revenue was $16.00 billion which was short of the $16.83 billion estimate.</p>\n<p>Market Domination Anchors <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/josh-lipton/\">Josh Lipton</a> and <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/julie-hyman/\">Julie Hyman</a> report the breaking details.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more Market Domination Overtime <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination-overtime/\">here</a>.</p>",
      "summary": "Apple (AAPL) reported fiscal second quarter adjusted earnings of $1.65 versus a Bloomberg consensus estimate of $1.62. Revenue was $95.4 billion compared to the expected $94.6 billion. iPhone revenue was $46.8 billion. Wall Street had been anticipating $45.9 billion. Mac revenue and iPad revenue both topped estimates while Services and Wearables revenue fell short. Greater China revenue was $16.00 billion which was short of the $16.83 billion estimate. Market Domination Anchors Josh Lipton and Julie Hyman report the breaking details. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more Market Domination Overtime here.",
